      \field{abstract}{Substantial improvements in the performance of "particle-particle- particle-mesh" (P{\textasciicircum}3{\textasciicircum}M) algorithms may be achieved by allowing spatially adaptive mesh refinements in regions of high particle density. The cycle time under heavy clustering is {\textasciitilde} 5 times that for a uniform particle distribution: {\textasciitilde} 10-20 times faster than conventional P{\textasciicircum}3{\textasciicircum}M. The algorithm is roughly 50\% faster than a "tree code" while requiring significantly less memory.}
