      \field{abstract}{We develop a systematic derivation for the Limber approximation to the angular cross-power spectrum of two random fields, as a series expansion in 1/({\textbackslash}ell+1/2). This extended Limber approximation can be used to test the accuracy of the Limber approximation and to improve the rate of convergence at large {\textbackslash}ell's. We show that the error in ordinary Limber approximation is O(1/{\textbackslash}ell{\textasciicircum}2). We also provide a simple expression for the second order correction to the Limber formula, which improves the accuracy to O(1/{\textbackslash}ell{\textasciicircum}4). This correction can be especially useful for narrow redshift bins, or samples with small redshift overlap, for which the zeroth order Limber formula has a large error. We also point out that using {\textbackslash}ell instead of ({\textbackslash}ell+1/2), as is often done in the literature, spoils the accuracy of the approximation to O(1/{\textbackslash}ell).}
